Generic pattern being save-shift-restore. Save `k' elements into fifo, shift other elements and trample over these then restore fifo contents at new location.
===================================================
LeftRotate(A, k)
// where k is the size of the temporary buffer provided to you
j = len - k;

for (i = 0; i < len; ++i) {
    if (i < k) {
       T[i] = A[i];
    } else {
      A[i-k] = A[i];
    }   
}

i = 0;
for (t = j; t < len; t++) {
    A[t] = T[i++];
}


RightRotate(A, k)
// Save 'k' elements
x = 0;
for (i = k; i < len; i++) {
  T[x++] = A[i];
}

// Shift
for ( i = j - 1; i >= 0; i--) {
    A[i + k] = A[i];
}

// Restore
for (i = 0; i < k; i++) {
    A[i] = T[i];
}

